{"path":"ranges/drop_view/drop_view","title":"std::ranges::drop_view<V>::drop_view","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::ranges::drop_view&lt;V&gt;::</span>drop_view","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/ranges/drop_view/drop_view","section":"ranges","kind":"page","summary":"The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">drop_view<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> requires <a href=\"/w/cpp/concepts/default_initializable\"><span class=\"kw2965\">std::<span class=\"me2\">default_initializable</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"kw1\">default</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw1\">explicit</span> drop_view<span class=\"br0\">(</span> V base, <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/range_size_t\"><span class=\"kw2910\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">range_difference_t</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>V<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> count <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Constructs a <code>drop_view</code>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> Default constructor. <a href=\"/w/cpp/language/value_initialization\">Value-initializes</a> the underlying view <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/drop_view#Data_members\"><code><i>base_</i></code></a> and initializes the count <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/drop_view#Data_members\"><code><i>count_</i></code></a> to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code>. After construction, <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/drop_view/base\"><code>base()</code></a> returns a copy of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">V<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> and <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/drop_view/size\"><code>size()</code></a> equals to the size of the underlying view.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> Initializes the underlying view <code><i>base_</i></code> with <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">move</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>base<span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> and the count <code><i>count_</i></code> with <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">count</span></code>. After construction, <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/drop_view/base\"><code>base()</code></a> returns a copy of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">base</span></code> and <a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/drop_view/size\"><code>size()</code></a> returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/size\"><span class=\"kw3118\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">size</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>base<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> count</span></code> if the size of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">base</span></code> is not less than <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">count</span></code>, or <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code> otherwise.</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> base\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the underlying view\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> count\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> number of elements to skip\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;algorithm&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;array&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iterator&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;ranges&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/array\"><span class=\"kw1276\">std::<span class=\"me2\">array</span></span></a> hi<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">'H'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'e'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'l'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'l'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'o'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">','</span>,\n                            <span class=\"st0\">' '</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'C'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'+'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'+'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'2'</span>, <span class=\"st0\">'0'</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/ranges/for_each\"><span class=\"kw3007\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">for_each</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>hi, <span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> c<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">{</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> c<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> n <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/distance\"><span class=\"kw678\">std::<span class=\"me2\">distance</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>hi.<span class=\"me1\">cbegin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/ranges/find\"><span class=\"kw3002\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">find</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>hi, <span class=\"st0\">'C'</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> cxx <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/ranges/drop_view\"><span class=\"kw2945\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">drop_view</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">{</span>hi, n<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/ranges/for_each\"><span class=\"kw3007\">ranges::<span class=\"me2\">for_each</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>cxx, <span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> c<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">{</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> c<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Hello, C++20\nC++20</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue3714\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 3714</a><br>(<a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://wg21.link/P2711R1\" data-external=\"1\">P2711R1</a>)\n</td>\n<td>C++20\n</td>\n<td>the multi-parameter constructor was not explicit\n</td>\n<td>made explicit\n</td></tr></table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"ranges","title":"Ranges library (since C++20)"},{"path":"ranges/drop_view","title":"std::ranges::views::drop, std::ranges::drop_view"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::ranges::drop_view<V>::drop_view","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++20. Constructs a drop_view."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"base, count"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"Defect reports","note":"The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards."}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":212,"codeBlockCount":2}
